Hi Gauthami, payeeBank.address is mapped, it is not a todo. The summary table only said "agent rule" for the creditor agent and did not spell the address out, so I can see why it looked missing. I have added the rows to the README.

Payee bank to pain.001 V11 (CdtTrfTxInf/CdtrAgt):
- payeeBank.swiftBankIdentifierCode -> FinInstnId/BICFI
- payeeBank.bankSystemIdentifier + payeeBank.bankCode -> FinInstnId/ClrSysMmbId (ClrSysId/Cd + MmbId; a 9-digit code with no system id is treated as USABA)
- payeeBank.legalEntityIdentifier -> FinInstnId/LEI
- payeeBank.bankName -> FinInstnId/Nm
- payeeBank.address -> FinInstnId/PstlAdr
- payeeBank.bankAccountNumber -> CdtrAgtAcct/Id/Othr/Id

Address fields (same rule for every party and agent address):
- department -> Dept (70)
- subDepartment -> SubDept (70)
- streetName -> StrtNm (70)
- buildingNumber -> BldgNb (16)
- buildingName -> BldgNm (35)
- floor -> Flr (70)
- postalBox -> PstBx (16)
- room -> Room (70)
- postalCode -> PstCd (16)
- city, else townName -> TwnNm (35)
- townLocationName -> TwnLctnNm (35)
- districtName -> DstrctNm (35)
- stateCode, else stateProvince -> CtrySubDvsn (35)
- countryCode -> Ctry (2 letters)
- addressLine1 to addressLine4 -> AdrLine (70 each)
Not read: countryName, proxyAccountIdentification.

What is required: nothing in the address. In the V11 schema the creditor agent is optional, and inside it BICFI, ClrSysMmbId, LEI, Nm and PstlAdr are all optional, as is every address field. The mapper writes PstlAdr only when the address has at least one value, and does not fail when it is empty. In the FIS sample requests the creditor agent is just the USABA member id for bank and customer transfers; only the drawdown sample carries a structured address on it (department, subDepartment, streetName, buildingNumber, postCode, townName, countrySubDivision, country). Whether OPF requires an agent address per rail is still an open question with FIS.

One thing for your addendum task: the mapper reads only the payment object. It does not read the addendum. So an address that exists only in the addendum will not reach pain.001 today. Either it gets copied into payeeBank.address before the call to Wire Rail II, or we extend Wire Rail II to take the addendum. Worth a quick chat so we pick one.

Code: in bank-wire-object-mapper, the creditor agent is built from payload.getPayeeBank() in CreditTransferBuilder, the agent fields are in AgentMapper.agent(...), and the address fields are in PostalAddressMapper.map(...). I am moving the mapping to MapStruct this week; after that it is all in one file, mappers/WireCreditTransferPain001V11, methods toFinancialInstitution and toPostalAddress.
